outcome:
Follow-up from the tm-5gi4 phase 1 review pair on input c6140c01 (Claude Low, 2026-09-27; landed as acd7740). It was also on Opus's own list of candidates.

Four assertions rely on 'the fixture's workdir is no Git worktree':
- the unmeasured notice (src/tests/acceptance_evaluation.rs around line 1725);
- the joined notice (around line 4717);
- 'no sourceFingerprint' in the same-session request test;
- acceptance_submit_declares_nothing_when_the_revision_cannot_be_taken_again.

engram_worktree_root_path climbs to any ancestor that holds .git. If TERMAL_TEST_USER_TEMP or TEMP points inside a repository (which the repo's keep-scratch-under-.tmp rule invites), the capture measures the whole enclosing tree. That is slow, and it flips these assertions: the submit test gets a 409 instead of 'declares nothing'.

Fix: build the unmeasured case deterministically, not by where the temp folder is. For example, use a fixture worktree whose index holds a gitlink, or one with an untracked nested repository; both fail closed. No test should depend on the temp root's ancestry.
